[[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The integrated services control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              manages the operation\nof the electric front windows.</p><p>The direct supply from the battery for control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               specific to the electric windows (pin 15 and 16\nof connector A) arrives from the line protected by maxifuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J/B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (of \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99) and fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F12</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\njunction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while the supply controlled by the ignition\nreaches pin 7 of connector B from the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; \npins 4 and 20 of connector A provide the reference earth for the\npassenger and driver&#x27;s electric windows, respectively.</p><p>The switches \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (driver&#x27;s electric\nwindow), \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (passenger electric window on driver&#x27;s door)\nand \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (passenger electric windoe on passenger front door) receive\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT/A) from the line from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99, and are earthed \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : in this way they are also lit\nup when the ignition is switched on.</p><p>When the switches are operated, they send control signals (positive and negative) to control unit M40:</p><ul><li>at pins 10 and 11 of connector A from switch <strong>H40</strong> ;</li><li>at pins 5 and 18 of connector A from switch <strong>H41</strong> ;</li><li>at pins 2 and 6 of connector A from switch <strong>H50</strong> ;</li></ul><p>The control unit M40 operates the electric windows on the basis of the logic described previously:</p><ul><li>from pins 8 and 9 of connector A it sends commands to\nthe driver&#x27;s electric window motor <strong>N60</strong></li><li>from pins 1and 3 of connector A it sends commands to the\npassenger electric window motor <strong>N61.</strong></li></ul><p>When the positive and negative signals are\nreversed, the motor&#x27;s direction of rotation is also reversed.</p>"]]